3.34:
“The stars shone in their watches, and rejoiced; 
When He calls them, they say, ‘Here we are.’ 
And so with gladness they showed light unto He who made them.”

4.1:
This is the Book of the Commands of Elohim, and the Torah that endures forever; 
All those who guard it shall attain ḥai; 
But those who leave it shall die.

4.9:
For when she saw the wrath of Elohim coming upon you, she said, 
“Hear, O you who dwell around Tsiyon, 
Elohim has brought upon me great mourning;

4.12:
“Let no man rejoice over me, a widow, and forsaken by many, 
Who for the sins of my children am left laid waste; 
Because they departed from the Torah of Elohim.

4.22:
“For my expectancy is in the Everlasting, that He shall save you; 
And joy has come to me from the Qadosh One, 
Because of the kindness which shall soon come to you from the Everlasting, our Savior.

4.25:
“My children, patiently endure the wrath that has come upon you from Elohim; 
For your enemy has persecuted you; 
But shortly you shall see his destruction, 
And shall tread upon his neck.

5.6:
For they departed from you on foot, and were led away by their enemies; 
But Elohim brings them to you exalted with esteem, 
As children of the reign.
